es-quote1", "translation": "the white-gleaming host rises against the city"}, {"id": "leukoprepes-word1", "translation": "the white-shielded people rises up, well-prepared"}, {"id": "leukoprepes-word2", "translation": "M ) pursuing against the city"}, {"id": "leukopteros-orth1", "translation": "white-winged"}, {"id": "leukopteros-def1", "translation": "flying with white wings"}, {"id": "leukopteros-quote1", "translation": "with white-winged snow"}, {"id": "leukopolos-orth1", "translation": "with white horses"}, {"id": "leukopolos-def1", "translation": "drawn by white horses"}, {"id": "leukopolos-quote1", "translation": "white-horsed day"}, {"id": "leukos-orth1", "translation": "white, bright"}, {"id": "leukos-def1", "translation": "bright"}, {"id": "leukos-def2", "translation": "white"}, {"id": "leukos-quote1", "translation": "white day from black-robed night"}, {"id": "leukos-quote2", "translation": "throughout the white day"}, {"id": "leukos-quote3", "translation": "white water"}, {"id": "leukos-quote4", "translation": "white, drinkable milk"}, {"id": "leukos-quote5", "translation": "and white temples to rise up with this disease"}, {"id": "leukos-quote6", "translation": "from white robes"}, {"id": "leukos-quote7", "translation": "for with white and black fates"}, {"id": "leukos-quote8", "translation": "white, why not, and well cooked is the pig"}, {"id": "leukostephes-orth1", "translation": "white-crowned"}, {"id": "leukostephes-def1", "translation": "crowned with white wool"}, {"id": "leukostephes-quote1", "translation": "white-crowned suppliant branches"}, {"id": "leukostephes-quote2", "translation": "holding white-crowned, freshly plucked branches"}, {"id": "leuros-orth1", "translation": "smooth, level"}, {"id": "leuros-def1", "translation": "smooth, level"}, {"id": "leuros-note1", "translation": "where the schol. explains it by πλατεῖς [broad] (i.e. wide-spreading)."}, {"id": "leuros-quote1", "translation": "the smooth fields of Sicily rich in fruit"}, {"id": "leuros-quote2", "translation": "the smooth path of the air"}, {"id": "leuros-quote3", "translation": "through the smooth grove"}, {"id": "leuros-word1", "translation": "broad"}, {"id": "leusimos-orth1", "translation": "stoned, deserving stoning"}, {"id": "leusimos-def1", "translation": "stoned, deserving stoning"}, {"id": "leusimos-def2", "translation": "connected with stoning"}, {"id": "leusimos-quote1", "translation": "of a victim to be stoned"}, {"id": "leusimos-quote2", "translation": "publicly cast out – curses of stoning"}, {"id": "leusmos-orth1", "translation": "stoning"}, {"id": "leusmos-def1", "translation": "stoning"}, {"id": "leusmos-quote1", "translation": "stoning with stones"}, {"id": "leusso-orth1", "translation": "I see"}, {"id": "leusso-def1", "translation": "I see"}, {"id": "leusso-quote1", "translation": "I see, Prometheus"}, {"id": "leusso-quote2", "translation": "Whom shall I say I see?"}, {"id": "leusso-quote3", "translation": "and with eyes seeing the dark glare of the murderous serpent"}, {"id": "leusso-quote4", "translation": "and seeing my wife near the tomb I am afraid"}, {"id": "leusso-quote5", "translation": "while you saw the rays of the sun"}, {"id": "leusso-quote6", "translation": "What do I see?"}, {"id": "leusso-quote7", "translation": "and he saw everything"}, {"id": "leusso-quote8", "translation": "and I see the crowd of shield-bearers and spear-shakers"}, {"id": "leusso-quote9", "translation": "I shudder seeing these shadowy seats"}, {"id": "leusso-quote10", "translation": "these things you see"}, {"id": "leuster-orth1", "translation": "stoner"}, {"id": "leuster-def1", "translation": "stoner"}, {"id": "leuster-note1", "translation": "i.e. death brought about by stoning."}, {"id": "leuster-quote1", "translation": "he will not escape the fate of stoning by the people"}, {"id": "lechaios-orth1", "translation": "lying in the nest"}, {"id": "lechaios-def1", "translation": "lying in the nest"}, {"id": "lechaios-quote1", "translation": "as someone fears for her children, the all-nurturing dove fears for the serpents lying in the nest (thus Lachmann for λεχέων) that bring evil beds"}, {"id": "lechos-orth1", "translation": "bed"}, {"id": "lechos-def1", "translation": "bed"}, {"id": "lechos-quote1", "translation": "around the baths and your bed they sang the wedding song"}, {"id": "lechos-quote2", "translation": "the wife of Zeus's bed"}, {"id": "lechos-quote3", "translation": "alas, bed and paths dear to men"}, {"id": "lechos-quote4", "translation": "a cowardly lion turning about in bed, a stay-at-home"}, {"id": "lechos-quote5", "translation": "the highest ones of the beds whirl about"}, {"id": "leon-orth1", "translation": "lion"}, {"id": "leon-def1", "translation": "lion"}, {"id": "leon-def2", "translation": "Λέων was the title of a satyr play by Aeschylus"}, {"id": "leon-quote1", "translation": "of lions glaring like Ares"}, {"id": "leon-quote2", "translation": "with the dew of fierce lions"}, {"id": "leon-quote3", "translation": "and she reared a lion cub (thus Conington for λέοντα σίνιν) in the house, unweaned"}, {"id": "leon-quote4", "translation": "raw-eating lion"}, {"id": "leon-quote5", "translation": "a cowardly lion turning about in bed"}, {"id": "leon-quote6", "translation": "by the absence of the noble lion"}, {"id": "leon-quote7", "translation": "double lion, double Ares"}, {"id": "leon-quote8", "translation": "the cave of the blood-drinking lion"}, {"id": "leon-quote9", "translation": "of the fire-haired lion"}, {"id": "leon-word1", "translation": "Lion"}, {"id": "leorgos-orth1", "translation": "wicked, criminal"}, {"id": "leorgos-def1", "translation": "wicked, criminal"}, {"id": "leorgos-quote1", "translation": "to bind this criminal to the high-cliffed rocks"}]}